Sink accounts that need a login to the bottom of the picker

A profile that was never signed in (or whose directory is gone) used to sit
in the middle of the list with a `usage n/a` cell, so a half-finished setup
could take the row you meant to pick.

- profile::needs_login / sort_for_picker keep a stable order and move those
  rows below a `needs a login` rule in both the TUI picker and `ccw list`.
- Their usage column says `logged out` / `not set up` instead of waiting on
  an endpoint they have no token for, and they are skipped in the background
  fetch and in `ccw list`.
- The cursor starts on the most recently used account that can actually
  launch, never below the rule.
- 0.6.0, README sample and changelog updated.
